**Precedence:** [`.cursor/repo_conventions.md`](../repo_conventions.md) overrides everything below. Then other `.cursor/rules`, then `docs/v3_cursor_implementation_guide.md` and finalized plans, then `docs/v3_engineering_design.md`, then V2 guides/design (historical for V3 work), then archived V1 guide/PDF, then existing code (update code when conventions change).

[`docs/v3_engineering_design.md`](../../docs/v3_engineering_design.md) is the architectural source of truth when no repo convention or V3 guide deviation applies.

Project identity:
- Python service-layer backend named calendar_backend.
- Persistence uses SQLite through SQLAlchemy ORM and Alembic.
- Mutations go through services inside transactions.
- ORM models are persistence records, not behavior-heavy domain objects.
- DTOs/result objects use frozen dataclasses where practical.
- Scheduling components must be isolated from persistence.
- V3 adds FastAPI HTTP boundary for frontend integration; V2 scheduling/plan-tree behavior preserved.
- V3 prioritizes correctness, readability, deterministic behavior, and explicit invariants.

Do not implement V3 non-goals unless explicitly asked (see V3 design §2):
- No production authentication or multi-user tenancy.
- No OS-level notification delivery (browser API is frontend).
- No external calendar sync.
- No server-side draft sessions for plan tree edit mode.
- No mobile native frontend.
- No sub-minute scheduling.
- No blocks on user-facing task calendar export.

Historical V2 non-goals remain in [`docs/v2_engineering_design.md`](../../docs/v2_engineering_design.md) §2 for V2-only work.
